    <category term="IBM 701"/>
    <category term="IBM 704"/>
    <category term="John Backus"/>
    <category term="John Mauchly"/>
    <category term="Presper Eckert"/>
    <category term="The Art of Computer Programming"/>
    <summary>In 1946, ENIAC and EDVAC engineers J. Presper Eckert and John Mauchly founded a company that became the Eckert-Mauchly Computer Corporation and developed UNIVAC I. During the 1950s, IBM introduced computers including the 701, 704, and mass-produced 650, while Fortran and Lisp helped expand the possibilities of programming. This marked the beginning of widespread commercial computing.</summary>
